<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO OUSTS ING AS TOP AMSTERDAM OPTIONS HOUSE.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO OUSTS ING AS TOP AMSTERDAM OPTIONS HOUSE.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN AMRO ousted ING</p>
<p>as the firm with the largest share of business on the</p>
<p>Amsterdam options exchange in 1996, the exchange said.</p>
<p>Figures published on Friday showed that ABN AMRO had a 17.28</p>
<p>percent share of all options and futures business on the</p>
<p>exchange last year.</p>
<p>This put ABN AMRO just ahead of Rabobank in second place</p>
<p>with 17.02 percent while ING slipped to third place with a share</p>
<p>of 16.25 percent.</p>
<p>The options exchange published the following rankings:</p>
